// qw_hud_ammo_readout — V2_HUD_Active bottom-center-above AMMO readout
// Interface: #include once into the qw_hud_active composer menuDef body.
//
// Mockup realignment (2026-08-16, TASK-70 acceptance #4 "Layout cascade"):
// the readout is moved BACK to the mockup's bottom-CENTER-ABOVE slot. The
// regions JSON (tests/visual/regions/v2_hud_active.json, ammo_readout) is
// anchored to the mockup at x640 y716 w160 h56; the bottom-right placement
// this widget carried (container right 1.94vw, digit leaf x0.934 y0.885)
// rendered the value ~75px BELOW and far right of that window, scoring
// SSIM 0.1105 against the 0.45 floor — by far the worst region in the gate.
//
// Canonical geometry — qw-screens.jsx:1290-1296 ("BOTTOM-CENTER-ABOVE —
// ammo big readout"), authored on the 1440x900 artboard:
//   :1291  container  position absolute, bottom:128, left:50% translateX(-50%)
//   :1293  label      Mono size={8} letter="0.4em"  "◆ ROCKET LAUNCHER ◆"
//   :1294  spacer     marginTop:2
//   :1295  value      DisplayText size={40} weight={700} letter="-0.02em" "88"
// Mono (qw-shared.jsx:233) = JetBrains Mono, uppercase, letterSpacing .18em
// default overridden to .4em here; DisplayText (qw-shared.jsx:222) = Oxanium,
// lineHeight 0.95. So the block stacks bottom-up from y=900-128=772:
//   value  40*0.95 = 38px tall -> top y734  (734/900 = 0.8156)
//   label  8*1.2   = 9.6px     -> top y722  (722.4/900 = 0.8027) + 2px margin
// That reproduces the regions JSON's measured mockup '88' bbox (y721..764)
// and its 160px-wide window (the 19-char label at ~8px/char advance = ~152px).
//
// 🔴 FULL-VIEWPORT LEAF RULE (hud-v2-redesign.md:26 — hard constraint):
// `hudElement` leaf rects do NOT resolve against their container. The .wui
// rect is back-filled straight to screen pixels against the FULL viewport
// (cl_wired_parse.c:1067-1070 WUI_BackfillToScreen: UNIT_NORM -> value *
// vidWidth/vidHeight), and the Clay-resolved x/y/w/h are then DISCARDED by
// the custom-draw adapter (cl_wired_ui_hud_register.c:493-495) — the legacy
// routine reads only its own config.rect. So moving this readout is TWO
// synchronized edits: the CONTAINER offsets AND every leaf rect. Both are
// applied below; the container positions the flow-text caption, and the leaf
// is hand-placed with an independent full-viewport rect to land inside it.
//
// Panel box: bottom 14.22vh (=128/900), left 44.44vw, 11.11vw x 5.56vh —
// the mockup's centered 160x50 block (640..800 x 722..772). NO background and
// NO border: the mockup's ammo block is bare text over the arena (unlike the
// health/armor panels, which do carry $hud_panel_bg60 chrome). The previous
// bottom-right revision's panel fill + amber right stripe existed only to keep
// the digit readable over the viewmodel HDR glow; at the mockup's centre-screen
// slot there is no viewmodel behind it, and any fill would be unmatched ink
// inside the scoring window.
// Tokens: $accent $font_mono $font_sans.
itemDef {
	name "hud_active_ammo_readout"
	type container
	position absolute
	left 44.44vw
	bottom 14.22vh
	width 11.11vw
	height 5.56vh
	direction column
	alignX center
	grow 0

	// Caption — flow text at the block top, mirroring the mockup's Mono label.
	// Kept on player.weapon.shortname (fed already-uppercased by
	// cg_wired_bridge.c:694-703); the mockup prints the FULL uppercase name, but
	// bg_weaponlist[].name is mixed-case ("Rocket Launcher", bg_misc.c:272) and
	// upper-casing it is a FEEDER change (engine LoC) deliberately out of scope
	// here. Explicit width PERCENT (NOT width FIT) keeps the proven bound-text
	// pattern — a FIT-width bound text node mis-measures into garbled glyphs.
	itemDef { type 0 rect 0 0 11.11vw 1.07vh height FIT width PERCENT 11.11vw bind "player.weapon.shortname" text "WPN" textalign 1 font $font_mono 8 letterspacing 3.2 forecolor $accent decoration visible 1 grow 0 }

	// Value — the mockup's DisplayText 40 "88", horizontally CENTERED on the
	// artboard midline (x720 = 0.5) and topped at y734 (= 0.8156). textalign 1
	// (CENTER) makes x the centre anchor; fontsize h drops 46 -> 40 to match the
	// mockup size exactly (the old 46 was the health/armor panel size, and is the
	// "~2x taller" term in the regions JSON diagnosis). Width term keeps the
	// sibling panels' 40:46 w:h ratio -> 35.
	// The mockup draws NO bar and NO icon in this block (qw-screens.jsx:1292-1296
	// is label + value only), so both leaves are dropped rather than relocated —
	// they were bottom-right-panel chrome with no mockup counterpart, and leaving
	// them would put unmatched ink inside the 160x56 scoring window.
	// 2026-08-16: y 0.8156 -> 0.7912 was tried (moving the digits ~22px up to
	// match where the mockup's amber mass peaks) and REVERTED — it aligned the
	// row profile but SSIM went 0.2089 -> 0.2021, i.e. slightly worse. The
	// position is not what this region is failing on. Measured ink coverage
	// inside the 160x56 scoring window: mockup 41.3%, engine 1.5% — 27x. The
	// mockup composes a full block there (weapon label, framing chrome, a large
	// two-digit value); the engine draws one small number. No amount of nudging
	// or resizing a single text node closes a structural gap that large, so the
	// value stays where the layout intends and the region is documented as a
	// content gap rather than a placement bug. See TASK-70 notes.
	itemDef { hudElement "statusbar_value" bind "ammo" anchor BOTTOM_CENTER rect 0.5 0.8156 0 0 font $font_sans fontsize 35 40 textalign 1 forecolor $accent decoration visible 1 }
}
